<pdd-reason>scripts/start.sh is the one-command operator entry point, so it must reuse an already-running valid Mixxx endpoint and propagate that exact port to an existing or newly started playlist editor.</pdd-reason>
<pdd-interface>
{
  "type": "cli",
  "cli": {
    "commands": [{"name": "scripts/start.sh", "flags": ["--mixxx-port PORT", "--help"]}],
    "io": {
      "stdout": "selected Mixxx control port and editor startup status",
      "stderr": "distinct unsafe or unavailable conditions"
    }
  }
}
</pdd-interface>
<pdd-dependency>hands/mixxx_control_Python.prompt</pdd-dependency>

% Goal

Keep `scripts/start.sh` as the safe one-command startup path while treating Mixxx control port `9995` as a preference rather than a strict requirement.

% Requirements

1. Parse `--mixxx-port PORT`; reject missing values and unknown arguments.
2. Ask `hands.mixxx_control` to discover and validate the endpoint. Do not duplicate broad port-scanning logic in shell.
3. Reuse an already-running patched Mixxx on any validated owned localhost listener.
4. If Mixxx is running but no valid control API is reachable, report that distinct condition and do not start a second instance.
5. Start Mixxx with the explicit port or preferred `9995` only when no Mixxx process is running, then wait for protocol validation rather than raw TCP availability.
6. If port `8787` already serves the claw-dj editor, POST the chosen Mixxx port to `/api/mix/control-port` before opening it.
7. If `8787` belongs to another service, refuse to replace or connect to it.
8. Otherwise start the playlist editor with `--mixxx-control-port` set to the selected value.
9. Propagate the selected port consistently to Analyze & enrich, Build/Start mix metadata, and CLI live execution through their established callers.
10. Do not start playback and do not tell the user to quit a usable patched Mixxx solely because it is not on `9995`.

% Output

- Primary output: `scripts/start.sh`.
- Preserve POSIX/macOS-compatible Bash behavior and existing one-command UX.

% Verification

- Run `bash -n scripts/start.sh scripts/run_mix.sh`.
- Run the focused Mixxx port tests and playlist-editor integration tests.
- Verify explicit override precedence, validated non-default reuse, unrelated-listener refusal, and running-Mixxx-without-API refusal without starting playback.
